  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "What is the probability that a randomly drawn positive factor of \\(60\\) is less than \\(7?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{6}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Factor pairs provide an organized way to find every positive factor of \\(60\\). The smaller member of a pair is at most \\(7\\), since two integers at least \\(8\\) would have product at least \\(64\\). Each number from \\(1\\) through \\(6\\) divides \\(60\\), while \\(7\\) does not. Thus all the factor pairs are\n\\[\n(1,60),\\ (2,30),\\ (3,20),\n\\]\n\\[\n(4,15),\\ (5,12),\\ (6,10).\n\\]\nThese pairs contain twelve different factors. Exactly six, namely \\(1,2,3,4,5,6\\), are less than \\(7\\). Each factor is equally likely to be drawn, so the probability is\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{12}=\\boxed{\\frac12},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
